nd  new indication into covid19 and  i don't have time to go into these  details but  just want to illustrate here the power  of genetics  to identify four different  molecules circulating in blood which are  associated  potentially causally with cov19 and as  such  represent potential drug for uh  repositioning for kobi  indications  the the second enabling project as you  remember  is analyze the genomic architecture of  coding variants  including these human knockout  variations in the french canadian  population  and that's with the work that claude has  been doing in collaboration with john  ryu  uh john being at the astitude cardiology  demo here  the data shown here refers to 2500  exons which have been sequenced by  the mit and  what claude has done is looked  at all the mutations in these 2500  exomes and she found 9 000 mutations  which are abolishing the function of the  protein so  human knockouts they are rare most of  them very vast majority are found only  once  in 2 000 people and then what she did  it she looked at the relative frequency  the frequency in the fresh canadian  population compared to  the frequency in a non-finnish  european population and so if these  violence had the same prevalence  in quebec and in the european population  we would have  essentially a distribution around one  but we have here a second peak  illustrating enrichment  these variants and look at the numbers  1400 for instance here 1200 these  variants  are more than tenfold more prevalent  here than they are  in europe and when you plot them  individually  each dot here representing one variant  and this is the line of identity europe  french canadians if we had the same  frequency  we would be around here but there are  lots of variants actually which  now are known to cause diseases in our  french canadian population  and so it's now the demonstration that  we have here  unique population to work with  because these population have variants  that are found almost  no